<article class="env-lemma" id="0GDM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GDM">Lemma <span data-tag="0GDM">88.24.3</span>.</a> Let $S$, $f : X' \to X$, $T \subset |X|$, $U \subset X$, $T' \subset |X'|$, and $U' \subset X'$ be as in Section <a href="/tag/0GDB" data-tag="0GDB">88.23</a>. If $X$ is locally Noetherian, $f$ is proper, and $U' \to U$ is an isomorphism, then $f_{/T} : X'_{/T'} \to X_{/T}$ is a formal modification. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Formal Spaces, Lemmas <a href="/tag/0AQ1" data-tag="0AQ1">87.20.8</a> the source and target of the arrow are locally Noetherian formal algebraic spaces. The other conditions follow from Lemmas <a href="/tag/0GDD" data-tag="0GDD">88.23.4</a>, <a href="/tag/0AR2" data-tag="0AR2">88.23.9</a>, <a href="/tag/0AQW" data-tag="0AQW">88.23.10</a>, and <a href="/tag/0GDI" data-tag="0GDI">88.23.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>